### TeamForge Phase 5 API Tests (REST Client Format)
### Username Policy, Profile Completion, and Username Confirmation Flow

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@collaboratorToken = Bearer YOUR_COLLABORATOR_TOKEN_HERE
@incompleteToken = Bearer YOUR_INCOMPLETE_PROFILE_TOKEN_HERE
@flaggedUserToken = Bearer YOUR_FLAGGED_USER_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Check Username Availability (Available)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: { "available": true }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/username-available?username=new_collaborator_dev
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Check Username Availability (Taken - Case-Insensitive)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: { "available": false }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/username-available?username=ADITYA
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 3. Check Username Availability with Self-Exclusion
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: { "available": true }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/username-available?username=aditya&excludeUserId=u-collab
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 4. Create Normal User without Username (Rejected)
# Expected Status: 400 Bad Request
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 400, "error": "Bad Request", "code": "USERNAME_REQUIRED", "message": "Username is required." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "Collaborator"
}

###

### 5. Create Normal User with Duplicate Username (Rejected)
# Expected Status: 409 Conflict
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 409, "error": "Conflict", "code": "USERNAME_TAKEN", "message": "This username is already taken." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another Aditya",
  "email": "aditya.another@example.com",
  "username": "aditya",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "Collaborator"
}

###

### 6. Incomplete Profile - Allowed Route (GET /users/me)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: { id, email, profileComplete: false, needsUsernameConfirmation: false, ... }
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{incompleteToken}}

###

### 7. Incomplete Profile - Blocked Route (POST /tasks returns 403)
# Expected Status: 403 Forbidden
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 403, "error": "Forbidden", "code": "PROFILE_INCOMPLETE", "message": "Please complete your profile first." }
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{incompleteToken}}

{
  "title": "Blocked task creation",
  "projectId": "proj-1"
}

###

### 8. Complete Social Profile via POST /auth/profile
# Expected Status: 201 Created
# Expected Response: User profile with profileComplete: true and given username
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{incompleteToken}}

{
  "name": "Alex Mercer",
  "username": "alex_mercer",
  "university": "NYU",
  "role": "Collaborator"
}

###

### 9. Flagged Account - Get Me Returns needsUsernameConfirmation: true
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: Object containing needsUsernameConfirmation: true and username: "aditya"
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{flaggedUserToken}}

###

### 10. Flagged Account - Keep Existing Username ({ confirm: true })
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: { "success": true, "username": "aditya", "needsUsernameConfirmation": false }
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/username
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{flaggedUserToken}}

{
  "confirm": true
}

###

### 11. Flagged Account - Change to Taken Username (Rejected with 409)
# Expected Status: 409 Conflict
# Expected Response: { "statusCode": 409, "error": "Conflict", "code": "USERNAME_TAKEN", "message": "This username is already taken." }
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/username
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{flaggedUserToken}}

{
  "username": "jathin"
}

###

### 12. Flagged Account - Change to Valid New Username
# Expected Status: 200 OK
# Expected Response: { "success": true, "username": "aditya_pro", "needsUsernameConfirmation": false }
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me/username
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{flaggedUserToken}}

{
  "username": "aditya_pro"
}
